    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41008" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιστένω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>groan</i> or <i>sigh at</i> or <i>in answer</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ δ᾽ ἔστενε δῆμος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					24.776
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπέστενε δ᾽ οὐρανὸς εὐρύς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Th.</u>
					679
				</span></i>
			; <i>lament over</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέκνοις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Med.</u>
					929
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Caes.</u>
				21
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>. c.acc.,
				<i>lament</i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Tr.</u>
				947
			</span></i> (lyr.).</div>
